---
# karakeep itself. Browsers arrive through traefik and prometheus scrapes it, both of which the
# baseline already admits — but one caller lives INSIDE karakeep's own role and the first census
# of this slice missed it:
#
#   karakeep-time-tagger — its `wait-for-karakeep` init container opens a TCP connection to
#     `karakeep:3000` and retries every 5s until it succeeds
#     (roles/k8s/karakeep/templates/deployment-time-tagger.yaml.j2). Denying it does not crash the
#     pod; it wedges the new pod in Init forever while the OLD one keeps running, so the workload
#     reads healthy and the rollout simply never completes.
#
# HOW IT WAS MISSED, because the same mistake is easy to repeat: the caller census searched each
# workload's name across the tree while excluding its own role directory, to filter out the
# thousands of self-references. That exclusion also filtered out every caller that lives in the
# same role as its callee. When fencing a role that renders several workloads, read the role's own
# templates for init containers and wait loops — `grep -rn 'create_connection\|nc -z\|nc -w'` over
# the role — rather than trusting a cross-role census.
#
# 3000 is the containerPort AND the Service port — verified 2026-08-20, they match.
apiVersion: networking.k8s.io/v1
kind: NetworkPolicy
metadata:
  name: karakeep
  namespace: {{ k8s_namespace }}
spec:
  podSelector:
    matchLabels:
      app: karakeep
  policyTypes:
    - Ingress
  ingress:
{# Renders allow-all when the flag is false, so `netpol_baseline_enforced` is a real rollback
   lever. `| bool` for the string trap. Both explained in full in
   networkpolicy-traefik.yaml.j2. #}
{% if netpol_baseline_enforced | bool %}
    - from:
        - podSelector:
            matchLabels:
              app: karakeep-time-tagger
      ports:
        - port: 3000
          protocol: TCP
{% else %}
    # OFF. One empty rule admits everything. `ingress: []` would be the exact opposite and deny
    # everything, which is the easiest thing in this file to get backwards.
    - {}
{% endif %}
